  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Evaluation is simulation-only (SimAI/Vidur + AstraSim/NS-3) on a single 16-GPU, 2-leaf, 4-spine, 2:1 oversubscribed 100 Gbps Clos with LLaMA-3-8B Zipf Poisson traces (1000 requests/run); no physical RDMA hardware deployment or in-simulator comparison against CONGA, ConWeave, LetFlow, PLB, or packet spraying.",
    "In Algorithm 1, reservation table R tracks at most K occupied path keys rather than per-spine active flow counts or remaining bytes; once |R| = K (e.g., 4 flows vs Fig. 3's ~8 concurrent flows per spine), subsequent flows fall back to uniform random spine selection.",
    "Algorithm 1 pseudocode removes p_{k_i*} in OnFlowCompletion without checking flow ID, assumes OnRemoteUpdate loser re-hashing occurs before packets enter an active RDMA QP, and omits lease TTLs for crashed senders that never broadcast RELEASE.",
    "Protocol assumes predictable/invertible switch ECMP hash H(.) (plus multi-hop inversion for deeper Clos), PTP/Sundial-class clock sync within broadcast delay, single well-known dstPort (or per-(peer, dport) expansion), and preferably a separate low-bandwidth control network; control-packet loss and clock-skew failures are not quantitatively evaluated."
  ],
